<x:xmpmeta xmlns:x="adobe:ns:meta/" x:xmptk="Adobe XMP Core 5.5-c014 79.151481, 2013/03/13-12:09:15        ">
 <rdf:RDF xmlns:rdf="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#">
  <rdf:Description rdf:about=""
    xmlns:xmp="http://ns.adobe.com/xap/1.0/"
    xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/"
    xmlns:photoshop="http://ns.adobe.com/photoshop/1.0/"
    xmlns:xmpMM="http://ns.adobe.com/xap/1.0/mm/"
    xmlns:stEvt="http://ns.adobe.com/xap/1.0/sType/ResourceEvent#"
   xmp:ModifyDate="2017-03-01T22:00:31+01:00"
   xmp:CreatorTool="Adobe Photoshop CC (Macintosh)"
   xmp:CreateDate="2017-03-01T21:35:18+01:00"
   xmp:MetadataDate="2017-03-01T22:00:31+01:00"
   dc:format="image/jpeg"
   photoshop:Headline="FAO project GCP /RAF/424/GFF: Transboundary Agro-ecosystem Management Programme for the Kagera river basin (Kagera Tamp)"
   photoshop:Instructions="&amp;nbsp;"
   photoshop:Credit="Â©FAO/Marco Longari"
   photoshop:Source="&amp;nbsp;"
   photoshop:City="Kirushiya"
   photoshop:Country="TANZANIA"
   photoshop:ColorMode="4"
   photoshop:ICCProfile="U.S. Web Coated (SWOP) v2"
   xmpMM:InstanceID="xmp.iid:0ef38246-a316-4d59-9379-8dcda64e435b"
   xmpMM:DocumentID="xmp.did:0ef38246-a316-4d59-9379-8dcda64e435b"
   xmpMM:OriginalDocumentID="xmp.did:0ef38246-a316-4d59-9379-8dcda64e435b">
   <dc:description>
    <rdf:Alt>
     <rdf:li xml:lang="x-default">05 June 2015, Kirushiya, Tanzania - A soil testing session to which farmers of the Farmer Field Schools are called to attend. Through practical evaluations on-site, farmers can assess the conditions of their farm?s soils. Thereupon the superficial strata of the terrain are scoured for insects, whose presence or absence, species and quantity will advise the farmers whether their land is healthy (the presence of parasites or of non-parasitic insects is an indication of the soil?s health). Furthermore, the technicians of the Tanzanian Ministry of Agriculture analyze the humidity of the soil: the ground is compressed in a ball, which is an indication of proper humidity and therefore accurate irrigation. A knife is then used to asses the consistency of the ground and whether it can be penetrated by roots that are pushing deeper in the earth. This technique, avoiding costly lab exams (largely inaccessible to low-income farmers) provides the communities with hands-on tools to assess the health of their cultivations, prompting immediate action by sampling and comparing the efficiency of their farming techniques.  &#xA;The rich agro-ecosystem of the Kagera basin will benefit from an accurate management of its diverse resources: for example by avoiding land erosion and arranging for fire prevention; by managing the access to pasture land through rotation and secluded plots where the soil is allowed to properly regenerate; by guaranteeing access to Farmer Field Schools where farmers are kept abreast of new techniques as mulching and contouring; by introducing fire break lines, ditches and troughs to retain water that can filter through the soil and recreate a proper water bed capable of generating streams, etc. Farmers in the catchments can turn around their farming techniques, acquire tools to produce better results in farming and sustain their livelihoods. The natural resources of the Kagera river basin, which rises in Burundi and flows through Rwanda, Uganda and Tanzania into Lake Victoria, are facing increasing pressures and degradation as a result of population growth, the intensification of agricultural and livestock activities and unsustainable systems of land use and management practices. The basin?s land and freshwater resource base, its associated biodiversity and thereby human livelihoods and food security are threatened by declining productive capacity and resource value of the cropland, rangeland and forests and by wetland encroachment. The PDF-B grant aims to improve knowledge and strengthen capacities at local, technical and policy levels for the preparation of an integrated agro-ecosystems and biodiversity management framework - the Transboundary Agro-ecosystems Management Programme (TAMP).</rdf:li>
    </rdf:Alt>
   </dc:description>
   <dc:rights>
    <rdf:Alt>
     <rdf:li xml:lang="x-default">Â©FAO. Editorial use only. Photo credit must be given</rdf:li>
    </rdf:Alt>
   </dc:rights>
   <dc:title>
    <rdf:Alt>
     <rdf:li xml:lang="x-default">24824_076</rdf:li>
    </rdf:Alt>
   </dc:title>
   <xmpMM:History>
    <rdf:Seq>
     <rdf:li
      stEvt:action="saved"
      stEvt:instanceID="xmp.iid:0ef38246-a316-4d59-9379-8dcda64e435b"
      stEvt:when="2017-03-01T22:00:31+01:00"
      stEvt:softwareAgent="Adobe Photoshop CC (Macintosh)"
      stEvt:changed="/"/>
    </rdf:Seq>
   </xmpMM:History>
  </rdf:Description>
 </rdf:RDF>
</x:xmpmeta>

endstream
